{
	title: 'Quiet source updates and command-aware composer actions',
	spec: 'Restore the invariant that live source edits do not interrupt an opted-in web page, its draft, focus or scroll. The host still lazily builds and debounces source rebuilds, but pages requesting manual updates stay connected and receive a validated web-update event when their bundle differs, including after reconnecting to a newer host. Until the user reloads, one persistent reload control shows. On pointer-fine (desktop) pages it ends the composer help row, right-aligned: "ctrl+r reload" in the attention yellow (colors.help update), underlined on hover; it looks like a link but is a button with an accessible name, and Ctrl-R reloads too. Touch pages have no help row, so a low-profile reload button sits over the upper-right transcript directly below the tabs: it consumes no layout height and never shifts or shrinks the transcript, status or composer; 16px text, no border, a translucent black background, an accessible name, a visible keyboard focus indicator and a target at least 44px high and 44px wide. Keep it clear of tabs and safe areas, without replacing other notices. Only the button intercepts pointer input; the overlay anchor leaves text and scrolling interactive. Clicking reload fetches the current page; draft persistence remains intact. Failed builds notify nothing; remote terminal sockets are unaffected; legacy pages retain the code-4000 compatibility behavior. Auth revocation and invalid-protocol protection retain their existing reload/error behavior. In the busy web composer, Queue precedes Steer in visual and keyboard order. A draft containing a slash-command prefix (including bare /, but not an absolute file path) displays Run instead of Send or Steer and offers no Queue button or queue hint, even when busy or showing completions. Command submission remains immediate, never queued; Alt-Enter runs slash commands normally rather than presenting a queue action. Plain-message send, steering and queue semantics, touch targets, upload handling and focus retention do not change. Behavioral checks cover manual-update notification without disconnection or page reload, stale reconnect, legacy reload and auth revocation, draft retention, action order and command-aware actions.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Manual updates use an explicit updates=manual WebSocket capability rather than changing code 4000 globally: old pages retain their reload path, remote terminals are untouched, and auth revocation still uses 4001. web.refresh is the watcher rebuild operation and allows behavioral tests without editing shared source files; Bun FSWatcher callback simulation through emit did not invoke its native listener. Slash detection includes bare / and partial command names but excludes absolute paths. Verified Chromium mobile layout at 390px: 8px reload label above non-overlapping tabs, 24px by 44px target, draft and editor focus retained across repeated updates, and click reload preserves the draft. Physical iOS keyboard behavior remains unverified. The first full suite passed 1334 tests with one model-switch timeout; that host test passed in isolation.',
